00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540 align:start position:0%
 
initiating satellite scan  I've been playing battlefield games ever  since battlefield 2 it was 2005 I was 14  years old and I had a busted-ass PC that  would take forever to boot the game up  but oh boy did I love that game and now  I've played every battlefield game since  2142 battlefield 3 both bad company  games as well as the Vietnam expansion  Battlefield 4 hardline battlefield 1  bloody hell I even played a bunch of  Battlefield Heroes but in every single  game in the series you'd see the same  thing on the spawn screen the little  blue arrow representing one of your  teammates just straight up out in the  middle of nowhere  sometimes it being a soul player trying  to flank alone or steal a vehicle from  the spawn or a support using mortars  miles away from the frontline sitting on  an ammo pack but let's be real for the  most part it was a recon player sitting  on a hill somewhere a few feet away from  a respawn beacon  and even if it wasn't a lone player the  sight of small groups wandering away  from the objective on their own little  escapade was always kind of a  frustrating sight even more so if you  were unfortunate enough to share a squad  with these players those who couldn't  find the capture point if the flag was  stuck up their ass anyway back to the  point I really wanted to make and that  is during my hours with battlefield 5  I've noticed that the small pockets of  groups wandering the map are much less  common and the lone wolf is almost a  thing of the past the editions that dice  have made the classic battlefield  formula has paid off in a big way when  it comes to how the players at each team  worked together being that lone wolf is  not only much less viable but it's  actually a lot less fun now too no  matter what class you play as if you're  alone you're gonna struggle recons will  get spotted and kind of sniped by a  communicative team if they're sat in the  back assaults will burn through ammo and  health packs through a combination of  automatic fire and aggression  medics aren't able to put down the  weight of fire necessary for them to  take on multiple opponents especially  arranged supports like the mobility to  defend themselves from attacks from  their flanks and are among the juiciest  targets for enemy snipers communication  and teamwork have always been powerful  tools in the battlefield series that is  a fact that fortifies the backbone of  the franchise but now in battlefield 5  teamwork is essential and  that's why I love it you can beg you  yard the attrition system is something  dice have spoken about a lot during the  lead-up to Battlefield 5's release and  this is a big reason why it's more  important than ever to stick with your  team but it's by no means the only  reason for those of you who may be  unfamiliar with the way the attrition  system works right now the upshot is  that the solitary soldier is much weaker  in battlefield 5 than there were in  previous games they carry less  ammunition and fewer grenades they're  unable to heal to full without using a  first-aid kit and most soldiers only  carry one life-saving bandage and you  can pick up a few rounds of ammo from  fallen enemies but that's not very  viable in a sustained firefight  especially since it means leaving any  solid cover you may have all of this  lends itself toward a cohesive squad  being much more than the sum of its  parts there isn't a moment where you're  at a loss of a way to support your team  beyond taking down enemies assistance to  your squad mates breeds a kind of  positive feedback loop the ability to  revive your buddies regardless of your  class means that you can keep a strong  frontline and keep pushing the objective  supports throwing up defenses keeps the  squad safe and an appointed strength  medics thrown around bandages means that  other members can be a little more self  sustaining and even if recons can't hit  the broad side of a barn they can still  spot a flanker exact enemy positioning  with shots telescopes or flares the  necessity to work together even  influences the way vehicles are treated  now similarly to real-life military  engagements tanks need to be supported  by infantry turrets turned far too  slowly to effectively engage charging  assault troops if they get too close so  having that backup as part of a  four-person fighting group is imperative  to keeping engines running  their sense of purpose and the way  you're rewarded for sticking with the  squad breeds a kind of loyalty even a  camaraderie in some scenarios taking a  heavily defended conquest flag with your  squad at your side makes you want to  stick together for as long as you can  stay in the same server I've had moments  in a game where I've watched a medic  I've just randomly been squatted up with  rushed through gunfire popping smokes on  the move just to get me back up and into  the fight after seeing that you know  damn well I made sure they had ammo  aplenty and I'd picked their screaming  selves back up as soon as I saw them  down on the ground  buddhir time fine boy boss nice yeah  funny a funny dive no you haven't  cheers me on mucker  our field has always been grounded in  the idea of teamwork but it has never  had such an emphasis on it on supporting  the soldier your side and I think that's  the main reason why I love this latest  entry so much now I used to have a  really close-knit group of friends who  had boots up battlefield three nearly  every night but over the years we  drifted apart and we didn't gain as much  I found myself missing that sense of  working together as part of a unit  towards the same objective and while I  don't have the same group of pals  anymore I can now get similar  experiences with nearly anyone I'm  squatting up with because to me the  emphasis on teamwork has felt a little  lacking in previous battlefield titles  but now with the changes and additions  dice have made two battlefield 5 I feel  like players get to be part of something  bigger with each match whether it's a  friend or a stranger I feel like we're  working together and that's exactly what  a game of Battlefield should feel like  like a valuable cog in the 32 play a  machine that makes up your team as great  as the game looks as great as it plays  it's been a pleasant surprise to find  that it's actually the teamwork on  display that stood out as my favorite  element about the new title but I want  to know how you found it  do you feel the difference from  battlefield 1 and 4 and how do you like  to play in a squad let me know in the  comments section below or find me on  Twitter at irregular Dave I hope you've  enjoyed this video and remember ladies  and gentleman always thank your medic  by chance manga

